{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012SXYsj75zhg9hFpjYaPy1g","type":"tool_result","content":"### 2.7 Schema generation hook (`scripts/schema.ts`)\n\nThe config area owns the zod schema and a pure function\n`renderProjectSchema():string` in `src/config/json-schema.ts` that returns\nthe full `roast.schema.json` text (`JSON.stringify(value, null, 2)` plus a\ntrailing newline). This area owns the hook:\n\n1. `scripts/schema.ts` bundles `src/config/json-schema.ts` with the same\n   base options as 2.5 (minus banner, defines, and metafile) into\n   `node_modules/.cache/roast/schema.mjs`, dynamically imports it, and\n   calls `renderProjectSchema()`.\n2. It writes `roast.schema.json` at the repo root only when the content\n   differs, and prints whether it changed.\n3. `npm run build` runs it first, so a developer who edits the zod schema\n   gets the committed file regenerated and sees it in `git status`.\n4. CI runs `git diff --exit-code -- roast.schema.json` after the build, so\n   a pull request that changed the schema without committing the\n   regenerated file fails.\n5. The config area's drift test (generated text equals the committed file)\n   runs in the test bundle and catches drift when `test:run` is used\n   without a build.\n\nThe hook lands in M1, when the config area's zod schema exists. In M0\n`build` does not call it. During M1 to M5 the generated file must still\nsatisfy the Go `TestSchemaMatchesConfigStruct`, which compares structure\nand JSON types only, not formatting.\n\n### 5.1 Bundle smoke tests (spawn `node dist/cli.js`)\n\n- `--version` exits 0 and its stdout contains the `package.json`\n  version.\n- `--help` exits 0; its stdout under `LC_ALL=de_DE.UTF-8\n  LANG=de_DE.UTF-8` equals its stdout under `LC_ALL=C` (locale pinned,\n  2.5 caveat).\n- In a temporary Git repository with a toplevel `.roast.json` containing\n  comments and a `gate` section, `gate settings` exits 0 and prints\n  `timeout_seconds=` and `severity=` lines with the configured values\n  (bundled `jsonc-parser` and `zod` work).\n- `dist/cli.js` starts with `#!/usr/bin/env node` and has the owner\n  execute bit.\n\n- With a Node version below 22.18 reported (the startup check takes the\n  version as an argument), the check returns an error naming `22.18` and\n  the CLI exits non-zero; at or above the floor it passes.\n- The zstd `ExperimentalWarning` filter drops that warning and passes\n  other warnings through.\n\n### 5.5 Schema\n\nOwned by the config area: generated schema text equals the committed\n`roast.schema.json` (successor of `TestSchemaMatchesConfigStruct`). The\ninit area keeps \"the `$schema` written by init points inside\n`node_modules/@substrate-system/roast/` at a `.json` file\"\n(`TestInitSchemaPointsIntoTheInstalledPackage`).\n\n### 5.6 Differential harness\n### 2.10 Commands\n\nAll gate subcommands take no positional arguments (extra args -> usage\nerror, exit 2). `roast gate` with no subcommand prints help, exit 0.\nErrors that are not usage errors exit 4 (the CLI's generic code).\n\n**`roast gate enable`**\n\n1. Git root of cwd; failure -> usage error `not inside a Git repository`.\n2. `gateConfigPath(repo)` = project-config search starting and stopping at\n   the toplevel (only `<toplevel>/.roast.json`, a non-directory). Search\n   error -> usage error with that message. Not found -> usage error:\n   ``the pre-commit gate runs from the Git toplevel and finds no\n   .roast.json there; put the project config at the toplevel (`npx roast\n   init`) before enabling the gate``. The config is not loaded,\n   validated, or trust-checked.\n3. `install(repo)`, then `recordDecision(repo, enabled)` -- also for\n   `manual`.\n4. Output on stdout:\n   - `manual`: ``<hookPath> is not an appendable shell script; Roast left\n     it untouched.\\nAdd this line manually:\\n\\n    <manualLine>\\n`` and\n     stop.\n   - `installed`: `gate installed: <hookPath>`\n   - `appended`: `gate appended to existing hook: <hookPath>`\n   - `refreshed`: `gate refreshed: <hookPath>`\n   - `up-to-date`: `gate already up to date: <hookPath>`\n   - then, for all of the above four: `bypass one commit with: ROAST_SKIP=1\n     git commit ...`\n\n**`roast gate disable`** (no config required)\n\n1. Git root; failure -> usage error `not inside a Git repository`.\n2. `remove(repo)`, then `recordDecision(repo, declined)`.\n3. stdout: `removed` -> `gate removed from <hookPath>`; `preserved` ->\n   `gate disabled for this repository; shared dispatcher preserved at\n   <hookPath>`; otherwise `no Roast gate was installed; recorded the\n   decline`.\n\n**`roast gate status`**\n\n1. Git root; failure -> usage error `not inside a Git repository`.\n2. `inspect(repo)`; print exactly three lines (labels padded to align):\n\n   ```text\n   repo:     <repo>\n   gate:     <summary>\n   decision: <enabled|declined|none recorded>\n   ```\n\n**`roast gate settings`** (hidden from help)\n\n- Flag `--config <path>` (default: nearest `.roast.json` from cwd up to\n  the toplevel, the standard project-config lookup). Loads the config the\n  standard way (all failures are usage errors, exit 2; a missing config\n  names `npx roast init`). No trust check.\n- stdout, exactly: `timeout_seconds=<n>\\nseverity=<SEV>\\n` where `n` is\n  `gate.timeout_seconds` or 180, and `SEV` is `gate.severity` uppercased or\n  `HIGH`. Environment variables never affect these values (the retired\n  `ROAST_GATE_TIMEOUT` / `ROAST_GATE_SEVERITY` are ignored).\n\nConfig validation of the `gate` section belongs to the config area and is\nrestated here for completeness: `timeout_seconds` integer >= 0 (0 disables\nthe watchdog); `severity` case-insensitively one of `INFO`, `LOW`,\n`MEDIUM`, `HIGH`, `CRITICAL`; `offer` boolean, unset means true. Invalid\nvalues fail any config load with a usage error (exit 2).\n\n275:validated later (section 2.8 step 10), after the empty-diff exit. An empty\n279:### 2.8 Review orchestration\n622:src/cli/review.ts          runReview orchestration (section 2.8)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2c04a591-2f82-49dd-a2ef-471292a90a1e","uuid":"616cb27d-da81-48fa-9187-a823413ebc60","timestamp":"2026-11-18T19:44:34.476Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"### 2.7 Schema generation hook (`scripts/schema.ts`)\n\nThe config area owns the zod schema and a pure function\n`renderProjectSchema():string` in `src/config/json-schema.ts` that returns\nthe full `roast.schema.json` text (`JSON.stringify(value, null, 2)` plus a\ntrailing newline). This area owns the hook:\n\n1. `scripts/schema.ts` bundles `src/config/json-schema.ts` with the same\n   base options as 2.5 (minus banner, defines, and metafile) into\n   `node_modules/.cache/roast/schema.mjs`, dynamically imports it, and\n   calls `renderProjectSchema()`.\n2. It writes `roast.schema.json` at the repo root only when the content\n   differs, and prints whether it changed.\n3. `npm run build` runs it first, so a developer who edits the zod schema\n   gets the committed file regenerated and sees it in `git status`.\n4. CI runs `git diff --exit-code -- roast.schema.json` after the build, so\n   a pull request that changed the schema without committing the\n   regenerated file fails.\n5. The config area's drift test (generated text equals the committed file)\n   runs in the test bundle and catches drift when `test:run` is used\n   without a build.\n\nThe hook lands in M1, when the config area's zod schema exists. In M0\n`build` does not call it. During M1 to M5 the generated file must still\nsatisfy the Go `TestSchemaMatchesConfigStruct`, which compares structure\nand JSON types only, not formatting.\n\n### 5.1 Bundle smoke tests (spawn `node dist/cli.js`)\n\n- `--version` exits 0 and its stdout contains the `package.json`\n  version.\n- `--help` exits 0; its stdout under `LC_ALL=de_DE.UTF-8\n  LANG=de_DE.UTF-8` equals its stdout under `LC_ALL=C` (locale pinned,\n  2.5 caveat).\n- In a temporary Git repository w