{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChAyr1Wjt61yX9Qrw8MrN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0143rRxPZj2FFne9owghGdyS","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/nick/code/roast.ts-rewrite-05-project-config-and-gate-settings; python3 - <<'EOF'\np='AGENTS.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nanchor=\"- Shell hooks here also block heredocs and commands containing `env:` /\\n  `.env` text; write such files with an editor tool.\\n\"\nassert anchor in s\nadd=anchor+\"\"\"- TS config (`src/config/`): `jsonc.ts` parses into null-prototype\n  objects (`newObject`/`setKey`, so `__proto__` is an ordinary key);\n  `schema.ts` (zod) checks shape and types only, and `load.ts` keeps the\n  validated *input*, never zod's output (zod's record output turns a\n  `__proto__` key into a prototype). Range and cross-field checks are\n  plain functions in `load.ts` so Go's order holds. Editor-only\n  constraints (enum, pattern, minimum, required) go in `.meta()`.\n- `roast.schema.json` is generated: `npm run schema` (`scripts/schema.ts`,\n  run first by `bundle` and `build`) renders\n  `src/config/json-schema.ts`; `test/config/schema.ts` fails on drift.\n  Edit the zod schema, never the JSON file. Shared esbuild options live\n  in `scripts/esbuild-options.ts` (`bundle.ts` runs on import).\n- A one-off esbuild bundle of TS sources that pulls in `jsonc-parser`\n  needs `mainFields: ['module', 'main']` (its UMD build does dynamic\n  `require`). Configs the tests load as realistic examples go in\n  `test/config/examples.ts`; the schema test validates each with ajv.\n- The CLI loads config only through `loadProjectConfig(explicit, ctx)`\n  (`src/cli/config.ts`); `configHooks.storedCredentials` is where the\n  credentials area attaches its store.\n\"\"\"\ns=s.replace(anchor,add)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nnpm run -s lint 2>&1 | grep -B2 error; npm run -s typecheck 2>&1 | grep error; npm run -s test:ts 2>&1 | grep -v 'npm warn\\|npm notice' | tail -6"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":258,"cache_read_input_tokens":180876,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":258},"output_tokens":136,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2c04a591-2f82-49dd-a2ef-471292a90a1e","uuid":"3bf5d27f-b0cc-4fb4-9553-41cab01089a7","timestamp":"2026-11-18T19:55:16.076Z","request_id":"req_011ChAyr1G7SYJoosnupcSkt","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_0143rRxPZj2FFne9owghGdyS":{"command":"cd /Users/nick/code/roast.ts-rewrite-05-project-config-and-gate-settings; python3 - <<'EOF'\np='AGENTS.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nanchor=\"- Shell hooks here also block heredocs and commands containing `env:` /\\n  `.env` text; write such files with an editor tool.\\n\"\nassert anchor in s\nadd=anchor+\"\"\"- TS config (`src/config/`): `jsonc.ts` parses into null-prototype\n  objects (`newObject`/`setKey`, so `__proto__` is an ordinary key);\n  `schema.ts` (zod) checks shape and types only, and `load.ts` keeps the\n  validated *input*, never zod's output (zod's record output turns a\n  `__proto__` key into a prototype). Range and cross-field checks are\n  plain functions in `load.ts` so Go's order holds. Editor-only\n  constraints (enum, pattern, minimum, required) go in `.meta()`.\n- `roast.schema.json` is generated: `npm run schema` (`scripts/schema.ts`,\n  run first by `bundle` and `build`) renders\n  `src/config/json-schema.ts`; `test/config/schema.ts` fails on drift.\n  Edit the zod schema, never the JSON file. Shared esbuild options live\n  in `scripts/esbuild-options.ts` (`bundle.ts` runs on import).\n- A one-off esbuild bundle of TS sources that pulls in `jsonc-parser`\n  needs `mainFields: ['module', 'main']` (its UMD build does dynamic