{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChAzCyLbuxxRq6bbWQzwK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, and `npm run test:ts` pass, and the Go build and `go test ./...` still pass (including `TestSchemaMatchesConfigStruct` against the regenerated schema).\n\nTicket 05 is done: Roast can find, load and validate a `.roast.json`, and the hidden `npx roast gate settings` command works. All checklist items are checked and everything is committed except `.redeye/notes.md`. Final gates pass: lint, typecheck, `test:ts` (1112 assertions), `go build`, and `npm test`. One full `npm test` run failed a Go test in `internal/context` (`TestReadFileToolDoesNotBufferWholeBlob`), a package this ticket doesn't touch. It then passed 3 times on its own, and a second full `npm test` run passed.\n\n**Config loading** (`src/config/`):\n- `jsonc.ts` parses the file and records numbers written like `1.0` or `1e3`, so integer fields can reject them.\n- `schema.ts` is the zod schema. It checks shape and types only.\n- `load.ts` runs the checks in Go's order (version, literal `api_key`, `null` as unset, lone surrogates, the zod schema, integer lexemes), then the range and cross-field checks. Its exports are `findConfig`, `loadConfig`, `promptPath` and the small helpers the ticket lists.\n- `endpoint.ts` holds the endpoint rule so ticket 06 can reuse it.\n\n**Gotcha:** zod's output for a record turns a `__proto__` key into an object prototype. So `load.ts` keeps the validated input rather than zod's output.\n\n**Schema file:**\n- `src/config/json-schema.ts` generates `roast.schema.json` from the zod schema. The result has the same content as the old hand-written file; only the formatting changed. Go's `TestSchemaMatchesConfigStruct` passes against it.\n- `npm run schema` (`scripts/schema.ts`) rewrites the file only when it changed, and `bundle` and `build` run it first.\n- I moved the shared esbuild options into `scripts/esbuild-options.ts`, because importing `bundle.ts` runs its build.\n\n**CLI:**\n- `src/cli/config.ts` has `projectConfigPath`, `gateConfigPath` and `loadProjectConfig`. Every failure is a usage error (exit 2).\n- `configHooks.storedCredentials` is the hook point ticket 08 fills.\n- `src/cli/gate.ts` registers `gate` with only the hidden `settings` subcommand. The other subcommands are ticket 29.\n\n**Decisions to review:**\n- I added `ajv@^8` as a devDependency. The schema test uses it to check that the example configs (`test/config/examples.ts`) validate against the generated schema.\n- I read \"every example config\" as the realistic examples only. The lower-case `gate.severity` case is not in that list, because the editor schema is deliberately stricter than runtime there.\n- Specs 02 and 03 disagree on the `StoredCredentials` interface: 02 says `lookup` is synchronous, 03 says it returns a Promise. I used the synchronous version from 02 for now; ticket 08 should settle it.\n- I did not add the CI step that fails when `roast.schema.json` isn't committed after a build. CI isn't in this ticket's list of files to touch.\n\nI also added notes on these conventions to `AGENTS.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":311,"cache_read_input_tokens":187694,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":311},"output_tokens":789,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2c04a591-2f82-49dd-a2ef-471292a90a1e","uuid":"15fb6e5d-bfc6-40c0-946e-5acbc9ee67dc","timestamp":"2026-11-18T20:00:02.718Z","request_id":"req_011ChAzCy1X1ggFpEqPYjuZv"}
